 "pixel_frame": "Every pixel coordinate is [column, row] in the raw render as written to the PNG: x to the right from the left edge, y down from the top edge, no crop, no flip, no straightening. Mask columns and rows are integer pixel indices; the mesh projections are the renderer's continuous coordinates. Rows increase downward, so h = (chin row - point row) / (chin row - canthus row).",
