 "apex": "On the far side, the silhouette's greatest outward perpendicular deviation from the chord joining it at the far canthus row and at the stomion row, after the box filter; the filter's halo at both ends is excluded. The generic mesh has no distinct malar prominence, so on a plain render that maximum is the argmax of a flat plateau: plateau_rows (first, last), plateau_row_count and plateau_h (low, high) are the rows whose prominence lies within plateau_px of it, and the two mirrored turns' apex rows need not match. Only the hollow and bump renders carry a distinct apex, so assert apex.h against this oracle on those alone, and compare the two plain turns through the measure rather than through these rows. mesh_apex is the mesh's own maximum-projection apex (render_mesh.find_apex) projected, for information only.",
 "submalar": "Below the apex to the stomion row, the greatest inward deviation from the apex-to-stomion chord, after the same filter.",
